# mount.pdxfs — caps.decl
#
# Format: R90-XREPO.013.M1-001 line-oriented caps.decl grammar
# (paideia-os design/architecture/caps-decl-format.md). Replaces this
# repo's prior R53-vintage prose caps.decl (consumed_kinds narrative
# style) per the R90-XREPO.013.M4-001 adoption wave
# (paideia-os design/user/fs-tools-caps.md §2.2, paideia-os#2131).
#
# mount.pdxfs is a standalone CLI tool (a ring-3 ELF with its own
# `_start`), not a shared library: it performs its own syscalls
# directly rather than delegating every kernel touch to a linked
# library. See src/volume_cap.pdx, src/mount_op.pdx, src/mount_record.pdx
# for the call sites each declared kind below backs.

!KIND_USER                0x001   # invoker attribution (audit + elevate identity)
!KIND_VOLUME              0x003   # READ + INVOKE (mount narrow: volume_cap_resolve -> vol_kind_narrow)
!KIND_PDXFS_MOUNT_TABLE   0x004   # APPEND_ROW after a successful mount (mount_op.pdx)
 KIND_IPC_ENDPOINT        0x001   # semantic-pipe stdout (pipe_wire.pdx; svc.schema-registry not yet live, deferred)

# Notes:
#
# - All three mandatory kinds are load-bearing at exec time: mount
#   cannot proceed without an invoker identity (KIND_USER), a volume
#   cap to mount (KIND_VOLUME), or write authority on the mount-table
#   row it appends (KIND_PDXFS_MOUNT_TABLE). A parent holding less than
#   the declared rights on any of these fails the exec-time reconcile
#   with -EACCES per the mandatory-narrower-than-decl rule (format
#   spec §4/§5) rather than let this tool do partial work.
#
# - KIND_ELEVATE_CHANNEL is deliberately ABSENT from this decl.
#   `--force` on system mount-point classes (`/system/**`, `/boot/**`,
#   `/dev/**`) is expected to route through an on-demand elevate-broker
#   request per §4.2 of design/tooling/volume-tooling-ux.md (paideia-os
#   repo) and R90-XREPO.011 policy — the elevate cap is never held
#   ambiently at exec time, matching the `rm`-pattern the round plan
#   pins. As of the M6 landing (src/mint_wire.pdx, #22), the real
#   elevate-cap wire-through (`mint_wire_invoke` -> libpdx-volume's
#   `vol_kind_mint_elevate`) still sources its elevate_channel_slot
#   argument from a `.bss` placeholder (`mount_mw_elevate_slot`,
#   initialised to 0) pending a future boot-time `_init_caps` seeding
#   hook for standalone CLI tools — every system-tier mount refuses
#   with `MW_ERR_NO_ELEVATE` until that hook exists. This decl's
#   absence of KIND_ELEVATE_CHANNEL is therefore still correct: no
#   code path today expects the exec-time reconciler to hand this
#   process an ambient elevate cap.
#
# - KIND_IPC_ENDPOINT is optional: the semantic-pipe stdout binding
#   (src/pipe_wire.pdx) is a real call site but presently inert
#   (svc.schema-registry does not exist yet, see paideia-os#2000), so
#   the --dry-run / line-based sys_write(1, ...) rendering runs with or
#   without this cap. Reserving the decl entry now keeps the eventual
#   real bind a rights-narrow, not a decl amendment.
#
# - The KIND_VOLUME op-catalog gap (no dedicated `VOL_OP_MOUNT`
#   ordinal, only `VOL_OP_QUERY_*` + `VOL_OP_DEBUG_PRINT`) does not
#   affect this exec-time narrow: the decl reserves the rights band
#   (0x003 = READ | INVOKE); the kind's op catalog can grow without a
#   decl change (design/user/fs-tools-caps.md §2.2, §5).
#
# - M6 landing (STATUS.md, CHANGELOG.md 1.1.0/1.1.1) added six wire
#   modules (dep_graph_wire, lpv_errors_wire, mint_wire,
#   passphrase_wire, quota_wire, snapshot_wire) for libpdx-volume
#   v1.1.0's `--all` / `--snapshot=` / `--snapshot-list` /
#   `--passphrase-fd=` dispatches. No new KIND is CONSUMED by this
#   repo at M6 — three prospective kernel-side kinds surface as
#   documented gaps but are NOT declared above (no landed kernel
#   ordinal for any of them yet):
#     - KIND_VOLUME_SNAPSHOT (libpdx-volume-side ordinal 0x1A1, no
#       kernel-side match; snapshot_wire.pdx refuses SNAPSHOT_NOT_IMPL)
#     - KIND_DEK (aspirational; passphrase_wire.pdx unwraps into
#       private .bss scratch, no cap-install path)
#     - KIND_PDXFS_QUOTA (aspirational; quota_wire.pdx's install
#       helper is a documented no-op stub)
#   These will be added to this decl once their kernel-side ordinals
#   land; nothing this repo emits or invokes today depends on any of
#   them.
#
# - This decl is a signed input listed in release/manifest.pdxsig.txt
#   [artifacts.source] (`caps.decl blake3-256 = <BLAKE3-caps.decl>`);
#   tampering with a shipped decl fails signature verification before
#   exec ever reaches the reconciler.
#
# References:
#   paideia-os design/architecture/caps-decl-format.md — format spec (R90-XREPO.013.M1-001)
#   paideia-os design/user/fs-tools-caps.md §2.2        — declared cap-set for this tool
#   paideia-os src/kernel/core/cap/reconcile.pdx        — kernel substrate
#   paideia-os#2131                                     — fs-tools adoption inventory
